WEBVTT

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.620
Hello, glad to see you again.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.380
Today I thought we'd do an almighty winter picture,

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.640
and I wanna put a great deal of emphasis on the sky

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.560
and how we make big billowy fluffy clouds

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.020
that just roll and lay up in the sky here.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.810
So I've already covered the canvas with magic white,

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.530
and I'm gonna start with sort of a gray color here

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.430
made by mixing a little Prussian blue,

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.450
a little brown, and a little white.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.290
And we're just gonna start gently working this.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:29.940
Let it go.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:33.400
There we go.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.520
Let me just sort of work it around and around here.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.820
This is a winter sky.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.120
Bad weather's coming in.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.720
Okay, here we go.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.710
We just sort of bring all this together,

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.720
but we want this swirling churning action here.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.330
and very lightly back in here.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.880
Now we'll take our fan brush with a little bit of white,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.470
and we'll put just a touch of permanent red with it here.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.160
Okay, a little bit of magic white.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.180
Now we're going to start way back in the back.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.170
The cloud farthest away first.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.960
We'll start working this.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.900
Keep this brush moving all the time.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.910
Just let it dance and play and have fun up through there.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.280
Very gently we'll blend that.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.030
Okay, now we're ready to start working.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.250
Always doing the thing, it's farthest away first

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.270
and working forward.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.320
Hypnotize that a little bit, very gently.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.220
We don't wanna destroy what we've worked so hard

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.250
to put in here, we just wanna blend it together.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.640
Okay, and today I'm using two fan brushes.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.520
One so I can work with the darks,

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.880
the other one with the lights.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.600
Okay, we'll throw some old gray clouds in here.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:12.540
around and having fun too there he comes yeah maybe there's an old gray one just sort of laying

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.540
out here like kiss

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:44.250
work this one just a little touch into another little white cloud here and by

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.360
the time I've got down this low I'm getting away from the pink that I had I

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.720
just want the pink in the top to give indication that sunlight's playing

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:59.960
through there all these beautiful

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.550
Clouds just happen right up here in the sky.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.140
Clouds used to be something that drove me crazy

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.400
when I was a traditional painter.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.220
You'd work for days and days to make big fluffy clouds.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.710
And here you just sort of let it happen.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:18.910
Don't worry about it.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.310
Don't try to plan them.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:23.640
Ah, there's another nice one.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.430
Cause clouds are free.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.090
They have no boundaries.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.490
They come and go as they please.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:51.340
See.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.750
Really pushing that paint into the canvas.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.610
You want to grind the value right into the materials.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.750
When we're talking about canvas,

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.110
one of the things to look for when you're buying a canvas

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:20.340
to paint this technique is look for a canvas

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.540
that's acrylic primed.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.500
That'll hold the magic white on there longer.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.550
Keep it wet longer.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.660
And we depend on this being wet throughout the painting.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.370
Just another little fluffy right in here.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.080
Just wherever, just let it happen, don't worry about it.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.060
And here we're just putting some brush strokes in.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.240
Indicate light coming through there.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.530
Okay, maybe laying up here in the clouds

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:25.040
we have some little mountains that are just laying in here.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.210
Okay, we want these to blend right into nothing.

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:42.690
We're gonna lay these right in the clouds.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:50.210
Have a little light playing down through here.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.920
Just bouncing around, having fun.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.340
Here, right up to this peak.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.620
I want these to be far, far away,

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:15.870
just about disappearing right into the sky.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.250
We're gonna diffuse them by just tap, tap, tapping

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.410
right along, always following the angles here.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.970
Just tapping.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.720
they hypnotize them so they just disappear

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.940
right on back into the picture.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:46.150
Okay, we can just lay clouds all around them,

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:48.800
set them down in there.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:07:59.980
Okay, we'll work.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:29.970
those a little bit a little touch of gray in here now when you're at home

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.640
doing this and have unlimited time,

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.620
you can put a great deal more detail in here.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:37.290
This is just to give you an idea of how it's done.

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:44.830
Okay, let's have an almighty mountain.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.240
Let's come all the way down.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:52.630
It just comes right up through here.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:02.670
Very little paint.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.870
We're really pushing this paint into the canvas.

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:22.460
Take, pull that down.

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:25.970
This makes the next layer of paint stick better.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.000
I'm going to add just a little touch of Prussian blue here.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.660
Just so we have some shadows under the snow.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:07.020
Okay, now we can put some almighty snow

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:09.020
coming all the way down through this mountain here.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.810
And we're just gonna let it run and play.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.020
Just let it go.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.910
Okay, see how easy that is?

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.160
Just let it flow in there.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.760
We'll run some right along this mountain peak.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.230
And maybe here, since our light's coming from here,

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.620
this one's gonna be highlighted from the other side.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.920
Read a little valley maybe right down through there.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.980
We can lay in some shadows here

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.760
using just some Prussian blue and white.

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:25.410
That's nice.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:28.290
Any place you want a ridge to stand up,

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.910
all you have to do is lay a shadow underneath.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:32.480
and automatically it's right there.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.550
Shadows running down behind this one.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:57.900
Okay, now with a clean dry brush I'm gonna diffuse this,

00:11:58.100 --> 00:11:58.960
lay it in the mist.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:11:59.960
I want this to be mist.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.310
in the back, like it's very, very, very cold.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:08.290
I live in Fairbanks, it's not unusual for it

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.290
to get 60 or 70 degrees below zero.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.200
And it's always very, very misty.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:18.040
We have ice fog that forms and lays in between the trees.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.690
It's cold, but it's beautiful, so.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:29.540
Okay, let's take...

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.410
here, a little bit of the gray color,

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.330
and I'm gonna lighten it up just a little bit

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:37.020
with a little titanium white.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.340
There, nice color.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.590
Load this brush full of paint,

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.370
and we'll put a little tree way back in the distance here.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.320
I thought today we'd make these little trees

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.140
with a fan brush.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.440
We can make them with a fan brush,

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.060
one inch brush, two and a half inch brush.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:57.960
Today I thought we'd do it with this.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:08.170
You want these to be very quiet, very subdued, to give the illusion of distance.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.960
Maybe there's another one right there.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.870
We can start laying in a little bit of snow here.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:35.620
You see how that color comes through

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.930
and we use that to make the shadow effect.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:07.280
Okay, as I say, I wanna lay this in mist,

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.020
so I'm just gonna gently tap this.

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:12.020
I want it to be far away and misty.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.890
And we'll come forward just a little bit,

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.270
drop in some more little trees here.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:34.650
There we go.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.110
Just go back and forth with your fan brush

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.910
and you're sort of bending these bristles downward.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.420
And however many trees you want.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:56.910
This is your world, so you can put as many trees in it

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:57.290
as you want.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.590
But you notice these trees are a little darker

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.810
than the first ones we put in.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:19.710
Okay, now let's mist these up just a little bit.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:23.540
All I'm doing is just tapping a little.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.180
And maybe we got a few little bushes growing

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:40.300
right around here that just covered with snow.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.320
Put some magic white and some titanium white.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:52.320
Mix them together.

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.050
Thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:58.370
And then we'll just put these little sparklers here,

00:15:58.510 --> 00:15:59.830
just little snow covered bushes.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:28.100
I'll put a few little sticks in here.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.840
Okay, let's move over to this side

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.420
and see what we can put in here.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.180
Trees are closer to you,

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.580
they're gonna be getting a little bigger.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.880
And you need to, when you're making these evergreen trees here,

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.440
you need to leave spots open, in between the limbs.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.510
Birds have got to have a place to sit, and wind's got to get through.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.880
Don't kill all those.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:22.690
Get away from the little Christmas tree things we used to make when we were kids in school.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.820
Trees don't grow even, they don't grow straight.

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:39.160
However, it makes them happy.

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:43.110
According to the weather, the conditions,

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:44.790
amount of heat or cold,

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:48.000
all these things affect the way a tree looks.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.980
Maybe we want one right in the front.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:17:59.980
I just made this a little.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.300
a little darker so he stands out.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:03.670
Little baby tree right there.

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.200
Because he's a little darker, now he shows,

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.320
otherwise he wouldn't show.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.760
He'd just lay in there and be quiet

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:16.760
and you'd never know he was there.

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:18.910
Yeah, we know he's there.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.580
Gonna tap this just gently.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:42.540
And let's have this come down like this.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.180
We'll just make another little thing

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.090
coming right down through here.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:47.860
Change the angle.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:16.540
through. This is a very cold picture. I may have to go get my coat here in a second. It's about to freeze me to death. There we go.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.460
See, where the paint breaks,

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.720
shadows automatically happen in the snow.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.080
It's very rare that snow is pure white.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.040
You always have the shadows and you have some dirt

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.740
that chills through and all those little things.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:51.060
We'll have some of those nice little snow-covered bushes

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:51.940
on this side, too.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:54.330
Don't want this side to get jealous.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.410
Okay, a little magic white, a little plain white,

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.720
nice little snow-covered bushes.

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:36.040
Maybe, if we had such a beautiful scene,

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:38.110
maybe we'd need a little cabin about here.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.280
We have to have a little hundreds cabin

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:41.540
or something right out through here.

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:44.790
So first I'll take and scrape off the basic shape.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:48.200
This gets rid of all the loose paint, thinner paint,

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.920
so we'll have something to work on here.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:51.730
And we'll take that off.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.110
It's also a very good way to lay in your cabin,

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.930
to work on a perspective and to lay it out

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:57.030
exactly the way you want it.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.680
This is a general shape.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:03.260
The big thing is to get the loose paint off.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:08.580
Okay, now we'll take a little Van Dyke Brown,

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.600
and we'll paint this back eave back here.

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:15.040
Just like so, nice and dark.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:17.370
There we go.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:24.460
And we'll lay a roof on here.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.550
Just a little bitty cabin out here in the woods.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:40.800
Little snow on the other side.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:45.950
Maybe the snow's pretty thick,

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:49.240
so we'll lay it on there nice and thick

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:50.360
so it looks strong.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.680
We'll put the front on.

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.400
Okay, son of a gun, there he comes.

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:20.820
Okay, let's make this an old cabin,

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:24.480
so we'll just make it weather-beaten old boards.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:33.510
Lay some shadows on top of that.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.380
This is Van Dyke brown again.

00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:38.000
I'm just sort of alternating back and forth

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.450
between brown and white to make it look very, very old.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:46.950
This old hunter, he went out after a moose that was too big

00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:47.950
and he ran off with him.

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:52.560
So the old cabin's just standing here abandoned.

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:54.630
Better put a door in it though.

00:22:58.120 --> 00:22:59.960
Maybe a passing hunter would like to see.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:05.090
and stay here overnight, okay?

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:08.550
And we'll make this an old slab cabin.

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:10.150
We'll just put some boards right in there.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:40.620
And you can, if you want to push this back a little bit,

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:43.410
we can put a darker color on here first.

00:23:46.340 --> 00:23:47.840
We'll just push this cabin right back

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:48.980
into the bushes a little bit.

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:51.870
And we'll have some little bushes growing

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:57.080
right down like that, magic.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:18.090
Okay, maybe when this old fella lived here,

00:24:18.460 --> 00:24:21.240
maybe he had a little fence that ran back.

00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:24.560
Might have had an animal or two he kept in here,

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:29.890
so let's just put a little fence in this little fence.

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:31.260
It's running over the hill.

00:24:32.760 --> 00:24:34.840
We'll just let it go right on back over the hill.

00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:40.560
Just see the top of that one.

00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:53.640
Bit of highlight, then a little bit of snow

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:54.600
on top of the post.

00:24:57.300 --> 00:24:57.980
There we go.

00:25:04.440 --> 00:25:07.710
Okay, and then we can run some wire right down this

00:25:07.710 --> 00:25:10.270
and let it disappear right over the hill.

00:25:13.630 --> 00:25:24.420
So, okay, maybe a couple little bushes

00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:25.260
out here in the front.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.240
and I think we need some icicles.

00:25:31.740 --> 00:25:33.920
So we'll do just straight magic white,

00:25:34.330 --> 00:25:36.230
and we'll pull down some little icicles here.

00:25:37.990 --> 00:25:40.730
Using the liner brush, this is a number two script liner.

00:25:46.460 --> 00:25:54.520
Colder already, we got to snow a little,

00:25:56.710 --> 00:25:58.570
and let's put a few more little sticks here and there.

00:26:09.950 --> 00:26:11.450
This is truly an almighty mountain.

00:26:16.360 --> 00:26:17.040
Sticks here and there.

00:26:23.160 --> 00:26:24.320
Here and there are little indications.

00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:36.820
Okay, just here and there, we don't want to overdo.

00:26:37.460 --> 00:26:41.080
We want this to look very soft, very misty, far, far away.

00:26:43.280 --> 00:26:47.040
Okay, take a little thin oil here,

00:26:48.610 --> 00:26:50.410
and we'll just sign this happy little pitcher.

00:26:56.440 --> 00:26:58.220
And I hope in the last 30 minutes

00:26:58.220 --> 00:26:59.800
we have shown you something that...

00:27:00.350 --> 00:27:04.950
you can do very quickly a way to make some almighty clouds,

00:27:05.070 --> 00:27:07.750
almighty mountains, some fantastic things

00:27:07.750 --> 00:27:09.830
using very, very limited palette.

00:27:10.150 --> 00:27:12.590
We've used mostly blue, brown, and white in this picture.

00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:16.480
Almost nothing else at all, but it's a very effective picture,

00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:18.260
and it has a tremendous sky.

00:27:18.440 --> 00:27:19.540
You can work on this sky.

00:27:19.900 --> 00:27:21.860
Once again, you have unlimited time at home.

